WEBVTT

00:00:09.730 --> 00:00:12.150
<b>Let's do our best together!</b>

00:00:09.730 --> 00:00:12.150
<b>Welcome to the Cheer Association!</b>

00:00:09.730 --> 00:00:12.150
<b>Cheer is fun!!</b>

00:00:15.040 --> 00:00:16.410
Tatejima-san!

00:00:16.410 --> 00:00:18.280
Welcome to the Cheer Association.

00:00:18.540 --> 00:00:21.550
W-Wow. You even have snacks.

00:00:21.550 --> 00:00:24.240
Today's your welcoming party, Tatejima-san.

00:00:24.240 --> 00:00:26.140
Please, have a seat!

00:00:26.140 --> 00:00:28.460
Wow, thank you so much.

00:00:29.190 --> 00:00:30.300
We're glad to have you.

00:00:30.600 --> 00:00:33.340
Can I call you Kotecchan from now on?

00:00:33.340 --> 00:00:37.300
Tatejima Kotetsu

00:00:34.400 --> 00:00:35.050
Please don't.

00:00:35.050 --> 00:00:37.300
She's brutally honest
when she needs to be.

00:00:37.300 --> 00:00:38.310
Huh?

00:00:38.760 --> 00:00:39.880
What?

00:00:39.880 --> 00:00:43.260
Why can't you figure out what just happened?

00:00:43.260 --> 00:00:45.560
You're obviously responsible for it.

00:00:46.160 --> 00:00:48.870
Remember? She doesn't like her name.

00:00:48.870 --> 00:00:50.490
Oh... Oh!

00:00:50.490 --> 00:00:51.690
You forgot, didn't you?

00:00:52.210 --> 00:00:57.390
But it's such a cool name... 
And I wanna get closer to you.

00:00:57.390 --> 00:00:58.760
Can't I?

00:00:58.760 --> 00:00:59.450
But...

00:00:59.450 --> 00:01:04.400
I mean with, "Kotecchan," people 
might think your name is Koteko!

00:01:00.030 --> 00:01:01.910
<b>Kotecchan</b>

00:01:01.540 --> 00:01:03.370
<b>Tatejima Koteko</b>

00:01:04.400 --> 00:01:05.180
Koteko?!

00:01:05.180 --> 00:01:07.270
You just made her name even worse!

00:01:17.090 --> 00:01:20.970
<b>Anima Yell!</b>

00:02:38.010 --> 00:02:41.390
<b>A/V Room</b>

00:02:40.530 --> 00:02:43.760
Hey, this is the perfect opportunity 
to call each other by our names.

00:02:44.010 --> 00:02:51.150
<b>Tatejima-san</b>

00:02:44.200 --> 00:02:48.410
"Ta-te-ji-ma-san" is really long.

00:02:48.410 --> 00:02:51.150
On the other hand, "Kotecchan"...

00:02:49.270 --> 00:02:51.150
<b>Kotecchan</b>

00:02:52.020 --> 00:02:54.680
Four... That's only four syllables, right?

00:02:55.270 --> 00:02:56.780
My apologies.

00:02:57.080 --> 00:02:58.780
I'm sorry I was late.

00:02:58.780 --> 00:03:00.320
Oh, hey, Hizume!

00:03:01.400 --> 00:03:03.670
H-H-Hatoya?

00:03:04.450 --> 00:03:07.830
<b>Episode 5: Arm Motions With a Smile</b>

00:03:05.380 --> 00:03:07.830
I see. So that's what's going on.

00:03:08.240 --> 00:03:11.210
Calling each other by our first names... 
I think that's a good idea.

00:03:11.210 --> 00:03:13.120
Yeah, you might even start to like

00:03:13.120 --> 00:03:16.030
your own name more by 
hearing people use it for you.

00:03:16.030 --> 00:03:18.710
Only if you're okay with it, 
though, Tatejima-san.

00:03:20.070 --> 00:03:22.190
Well, what do you say, Kotecchan?

00:03:22.190 --> 00:03:23.970
You can call me by my name, too!

00:03:24.900 --> 00:03:26.970
K-Kohane-chan...

00:03:29.350 --> 00:03:30.760
Kotecchan!

00:03:30.760 --> 00:03:32.440
K-Kohane-chan...

00:03:32.730 --> 00:03:34.440
Grr...

00:03:34.440 --> 00:03:38.750
Well, now that Arima-san— 
I mean, Hizume is here,

00:03:38.750 --> 00:03:40.210
let's get started.

00:03:40.210 --> 00:03:41.320
S-Sure!

00:03:42.720 --> 00:03:44.250
You can stay seated.

00:03:46.560 --> 00:03:50.830
Kotecchan, we'd like to officially 
welcome you to the Cheer Association!

00:03:52.200 --> 00:03:53.900
Here's a cheer to welcome you.

00:03:53.900 --> 00:03:55.470
Ready, and...

00:03:55.470 --> 00:03:57.460
Come and join us!

00:04:03.590 --> 00:04:05.720
<i>I got to see the exact moment she changes!</i>

00:04:16.760 --> 00:04:20.650
K! O! T! E! C?

00:04:21.040 --> 00:04:23.980
C? H? Um...

00:04:23.980 --> 00:04:26.590
A? K-Koteccha—

00:04:26.590 --> 00:04:28.580
Um, Kotetsu is just fine...

00:04:32.880 --> 00:04:35.170
I-I'd like to do something in return...

00:04:44.390 --> 00:04:45.870
Where'd she go?

00:04:45.870 --> 00:04:48.110
Maybe she went to get something.

00:04:48.110 --> 00:04:50.520
I wonder why she opened the window.

00:04:53.300 --> 00:04:54.330
The piano.

00:04:54.330 --> 00:04:56.560
So she went to the music room downstairs.

00:05:08.150 --> 00:05:10.830
Thanks! We heard it clearly!

00:05:10.830 --> 00:05:15.560
How am I supposed to do cheer like 
this? I need to build up stamina...

00:05:16.760 --> 00:05:19.240
We have a good training method.

00:05:19.890 --> 00:05:21.590
You mean like jogging?

00:05:22.370 --> 00:05:23.880
Making pom poms!

00:05:23.880 --> 00:05:24.710
Huh?

00:05:28.360 --> 00:05:32.190
But we'll need to make 
Kotetsu-san's uniform, too.

00:05:32.190 --> 00:05:34.810
Yeah! Who knows when we'll 
get our next request?

00:05:34.810 --> 00:05:36.890
We might even get flooded with them!

00:05:36.890 --> 00:05:41.120
Oh, so those uniforms were handmade.

00:05:41.120 --> 00:05:42.900
We still have the pattern.

00:05:42.900 --> 00:05:48.030
I'm not that great at sewing... 
Do you think I can do it?

00:05:50.530 --> 00:05:53.800
Go, go, Kotecchan!

00:05:53.800 --> 00:05:55.750
<i>I've never seen a cheer push someone away...</i>

00:05:56.210 --> 00:05:58.860
Just kidding. I'll help you out.

00:05:58.860 --> 00:06:01.340
It'll be done in no time if we all pitch in.

00:06:01.340 --> 00:06:02.960
Th-Thank you.

00:06:03.290 --> 00:06:06.120
By the way, do you have a sewing machine?

00:06:06.120 --> 00:06:09.160
Oh, yeah. I have one I can use at home,

00:06:09.160 --> 00:06:10.970
so I'll probably make it there.

00:06:10.970 --> 00:06:12.170
What?!

00:06:12.170 --> 00:06:13.230
You're so modern!

00:06:13.230 --> 00:06:14.600
So you're basically a pro!

00:06:14.600 --> 00:06:16.240
H-Huh?

00:06:20.000 --> 00:06:23.480
All right, this is our first 
practice with four members.

00:06:23.480 --> 00:06:26.080
Th-Thank you for having me.

00:06:26.080 --> 00:06:27.660
I know I mentioned this earlier,

00:06:27.660 --> 00:06:30.360
but the first thing you have to do 
when you join is make pom poms!

00:06:30.360 --> 00:06:32.150
It works out your body, too!

00:06:33.160 --> 00:06:36.250
You wouldn't believe how much of 
a workout making pom poms is!

00:06:36.640 --> 00:06:38.410
Hizume taught me how!

00:06:38.410 --> 00:06:41.230
J-Just by making pom poms?

00:06:41.230 --> 00:06:43.690
Hey, let's move on...

00:06:43.000 --> 00:06:44.880
<b>Wants to run away</b>

00:06:44.880 --> 00:06:47.880
Who knows? It might become a 
tradition for the Cheer Club!

00:06:49.130 --> 00:06:51.140
<b>Tradition</b>

00:06:49.680 --> 00:06:51.140
<i>Tradition...</i>

00:06:51.140 --> 00:06:54.000
Wait, you're actually happy about that?

00:06:54.000 --> 00:06:56.200
We can make pom poms another day.

00:06:56.200 --> 00:06:59.260
For now, let's start with our stretches.

00:07:00.660 --> 00:07:02.800
Let your body relax completely.

00:07:02.800 --> 00:07:04.900
We'll start with our necks.

00:07:05.480 --> 00:07:08.220
Kotetsu-san, just follow what we do.

00:07:08.220 --> 00:07:09.400
O-Okay...

00:07:10.290 --> 00:07:13.240
One, two, three, four,

00:07:13.240 --> 00:07:16.270
five, six, seven, eight.

00:07:16.270 --> 00:07:17.760
Next, from side to side.

00:07:17.760 --> 00:07:20.680
One, two, three, four,

00:07:20.680 --> 00:07:24.050
five, six, seven, eight.

00:07:24.050 --> 00:07:25.750
Next, our shoulders.

00:07:26.210 --> 00:07:29.390
One, two, three, four,

00:07:29.390 --> 00:07:32.260
five, six, seven, eight.

00:07:33.110 --> 00:07:35.660
Next, we'll be bending and 
stretching our knees.

00:07:35.660 --> 00:07:39.310
Keep your backs straight and
lower your hips down.

00:07:39.970 --> 00:07:43.130
One, two, three, four,

00:07:43.130 --> 00:07:46.060
five, six, seven, eight.

00:07:46.500 --> 00:07:49.320
One, two, three, four,

00:07:46.900 --> 00:07:49.320
Kotetsu-san, your back isn't straight.

00:07:49.320 --> 00:07:51.930
I-It's not? I'm sorry...

00:07:49.320 --> 00:07:52.570
five, six, seven, eight.

00:07:54.350 --> 00:07:55.530
Are you okay?

00:07:55.530 --> 00:07:57.450
Y-Yeah, I'm fine.

00:07:57.450 --> 00:07:59.160
This is hard.

00:07:59.160 --> 00:08:02.220
No one gets it on their first try.

00:08:02.220 --> 00:08:06.680
You say that, but you did all this 
pretty well on your first try.

00:08:07.490 --> 00:08:08.550
Did I?

00:08:08.550 --> 00:08:10.380
You're amazing, Uki-chan.

00:08:10.380 --> 00:08:12.740
Uki's always been really good at sports.

00:08:13.650 --> 00:08:16.430
<i>But what does that say about 
me when I started first?</i>

00:08:18.020 --> 00:08:21.600
But I could never outdo you 
in enthusiasm, Kohane!

00:08:21.600 --> 00:08:23.310
Y-You think so?!

00:08:23.730 --> 00:08:26.310
<i>Uki-chan is amazing!</i>

00:08:28.840 --> 00:08:31.950
One, two, three, four,

00:08:31.950 --> 00:08:34.820
five, six, seven, eight.

00:08:35.360 --> 00:08:38.410
One, two, three, four,

00:08:36.900 --> 00:08:40.280
This is your first time, Kotetsu-san, 
so don't push yourself too hard.

00:08:38.410 --> 00:08:41.200
five, six, seven, eight.

00:08:41.600 --> 00:08:43.420
You're all amazing...

00:08:43.420 --> 00:08:48.090
D-Don't worry, Kotecchan. You'll
 be as flexible as us soon enough.

00:08:48.840 --> 00:08:50.960
You're not very convincing!

00:08:52.100 --> 00:08:53.820
Next, we'll work on our arm motions.

00:08:53.820 --> 00:08:57.470
Essentially, the poses we'll be 
doing with our pom poms.

00:08:58.020 --> 00:09:00.860
This is your first time doing 
this as well, Kotetsu-san,

00:09:00.860 --> 00:09:03.350
so let's try just watching in a mirror today.

00:09:03.770 --> 00:09:07.450
But should we be practicing at the entrance?

00:09:07.450 --> 00:09:09.050
If a teacher finds us,

00:09:09.050 --> 00:09:13.360
we can just say we were cheering 
for the people going home.

00:09:13.360 --> 00:09:16.070
Why would you cheer for people going home?

00:09:13.360 --> 00:09:16.730
Hooray! Hooray! Go-ing home!

00:09:17.140 --> 00:09:20.530
There are several types of arm motions.

00:09:20.530 --> 00:09:21.990
This is a high V.

00:09:22.640 --> 00:09:23.750
Low V.

00:09:24.400 --> 00:09:25.500
The T.

00:09:26.100 --> 00:09:27.250
Half T.

00:09:27.890 --> 00:09:29.000
Daggers.

00:09:29.590 --> 00:09:30.750
Clasp.

00:09:31.350 --> 00:09:32.420
Clap.

00:09:33.040 --> 00:09:36.860
There are others, but it's probably 
difficult to learn all of them at once,

00:09:36.860 --> 00:09:38.680
so let's just do those today.

00:09:38.680 --> 00:09:40.760
It's hard to get your 
hands in the right position.

00:09:41.150 --> 00:09:44.760
You have to always keep 
the backs of your hands

00:09:44.760 --> 00:09:47.020
and your fingers level.

00:09:47.020 --> 00:09:49.120
Um... Like this?

00:09:49.120 --> 00:09:51.510
Your wrists are bent.

00:09:53.960 --> 00:09:57.900
When you bend your wrists, 
your pom poms will sag.

00:09:58.530 --> 00:10:02.890
If you keep your wrists straight, 
the pom poms will look more beautiful.

00:10:02.890 --> 00:10:04.540
I see.

00:10:04.910 --> 00:10:07.560
The most important thing is your smile.

00:10:07.560 --> 00:10:11.290
If you can't smile genuinely from the heart,

00:10:11.290 --> 00:10:13.880
you won't be able to cheer others on.

00:10:14.280 --> 00:10:16.670
Got it. Smiles are important.

00:10:17.940 --> 00:10:20.300
We'll be doing our calls in turn.

00:10:21.000 --> 00:10:22.330
First, high V!

00:10:23.540 --> 00:10:24.310
Low V!

00:10:27.240 --> 00:10:28.480
Like this?

00:10:28.480 --> 00:10:30.490
Kotetsu-san, remember to smile.

00:10:30.490 --> 00:10:32.810
Oh, right...

00:10:33.350 --> 00:10:35.080
One more time. Low V!

00:10:36.680 --> 00:10:37.820
Half T!

00:10:42.480 --> 00:10:45.540
<i>Kohane-chan's smile is perfect!</i>

00:10:45.900 --> 00:10:49.620
<i>Maybe that's causing the contrast
between her upper and lower body...</i>

00:10:50.540 --> 00:10:52.540
<b>A/V Room</b>

00:10:53.330 --> 00:10:56.800
Next, let's do our arm motions 
along with some music.

00:10:59.590 --> 00:11:00.580
High V!

00:11:01.540 --> 00:11:02.680
Clasp!

00:11:03.280 --> 00:11:04.300
Low V!

00:11:04.920 --> 00:11:06.180
Daggers!

00:11:06.690 --> 00:11:08.680
Great smile, Kotecchan!

00:11:09.020 --> 00:11:10.690
Y-You think so?

00:11:11.290 --> 00:11:12.190
Clap.

00:11:12.680 --> 00:11:13.900
T!

00:11:14.480 --> 00:11:15.520
Low V!

00:11:15.900 --> 00:11:17.560
Half T.

00:11:17.560 --> 00:11:19.400
<i>Hey, this is fun!</i>

00:11:20.760 --> 00:11:21.930
We're getting more in sync.

00:11:21.930 --> 00:11:22.740
Yeah.

00:11:29.020 --> 00:11:31.880
We didn't have any time to 
practice dancing today.

00:11:31.880 --> 00:11:34.170
Well, the first half was 
the welcoming party.

00:11:34.520 --> 00:11:38.300
But it was pretty hard... 
Especially smiling all the time.

00:11:38.670 --> 00:11:42.710
I keep forgetting to smile because 
I'm concentrating on the poses.

00:11:43.350 --> 00:11:44.300
High V!

00:11:45.910 --> 00:11:47.060
Clap!

00:11:49.970 --> 00:11:52.240
You're smiling, Kotecchan.

00:11:52.240 --> 00:11:53.310
Really?

00:11:53.310 --> 00:11:55.310
Kohane, your call!

00:11:55.310 --> 00:11:59.800
Oh, right. Um... D-Daggers V!

00:11:59.800 --> 00:12:00.730
Huh?

00:12:00.730 --> 00:12:02.200
That doesn't exist!

00:12:02.840 --> 00:12:05.190
Starting over! Low V!

00:12:05.720 --> 00:12:06.780
Clap.

00:12:07.810 --> 00:12:08.900
Daggers.

00:12:09.750 --> 00:12:11.110
T!

00:12:24.560 --> 00:12:25.590
High V.

00:12:26.640 --> 00:12:27.780
Low V.

00:12:35.320 --> 00:12:37.480
Hey, are you okay, Kotetsu?

00:12:37.800 --> 00:12:42.740
M-My muscles are sore since 
I started in my club yesterday...

00:12:42.740 --> 00:12:47.000
Oh, right. You joined the Cheer Association.

00:12:47.000 --> 00:12:48.490
Morning!

00:12:49.940 --> 00:12:51.840
What's wrong, Kotecchan?

00:12:51.840 --> 00:12:53.500
Her muscles are sore.

00:12:53.500 --> 00:12:57.040
Ah... Yeah, we were like that at first, too.

00:12:57.040 --> 00:12:59.130
Kotecchan! Remember to smile!

00:13:00.280 --> 00:13:02.460
Yeah, but...

00:13:02.890 --> 00:13:03.970
High V!

00:13:06.360 --> 00:13:07.340
T!

00:13:08.690 --> 00:13:10.270
Half T!

00:13:10.270 --> 00:13:12.470
Wait, weren't your muscles sore?

00:13:12.470 --> 00:13:15.760
<i>They've already become conditioned reflexes...</i>

00:13:15.760 --> 00:13:16.760
Daggers V!

00:13:16.760 --> 00:13:17.590
Huh?

00:13:21.240 --> 00:13:24.090
And now Kotecchan's 
uniform is complete, too.

00:13:25.110 --> 00:13:26.560
What's the matter?

00:13:26.560 --> 00:13:31.450
I-It's sort of embarrassing being 
the only one wearing a uniform...

00:13:31.450 --> 00:13:33.370
Oh, you're fine!

00:13:33.660 --> 00:13:36.640
Uki's even more embarrassed. She forgot we change school uniforms today.

00:13:36.640 --> 00:13:38.000
Oh, shut up!

00:13:38.770 --> 00:13:41.090
Hey, wait a sec. Kohane...

00:13:42.290 --> 00:13:45.560
Did you come to school earlier 
on purpose because you knew?

00:13:45.560 --> 00:13:49.710
Of course not! I had class duties today, 
so I just came earlier for that.

00:13:49.710 --> 00:13:51.220
O-Oh...

00:13:51.220 --> 00:13:53.420
But I was kinda hoping you'd forget.

00:13:53.420 --> 00:13:54.720
You brat!

00:13:54.720 --> 00:13:57.980
B-But maybe Hizume forgot, too...

00:13:57.980 --> 00:13:59.560
Sorry I'm late.

00:14:02.230 --> 00:14:03.730
What's the matter?

00:14:04.090 --> 00:14:07.740
Oh, we just noticed you remembered 
that we switch uniforms today.

00:14:07.740 --> 00:14:09.770
Uki completely forgot.

00:14:10.230 --> 00:14:11.240
Oh...

00:14:11.240 --> 00:14:16.520
I had actually forgotten this morning, 
but my brother reminded me...

00:14:16.900 --> 00:14:19.370
That it'd be a disservice 
to the world to lose even

00:14:19.370 --> 00:14:21.610
one day when high school 
girls get to wear less clothes.

00:14:21.610 --> 00:14:23.210
You can always count on your older bro.

00:14:23.210 --> 00:14:26.890
Oh, I'm glad you're all here.

00:14:26.890 --> 00:14:28.970
We've actually gotten a request.

00:14:29.310 --> 00:14:30.970
A cheer request?

00:14:30.970 --> 00:14:35.470
We'll be hearing from them 
shortly in the home ec room.

00:14:35.470 --> 00:14:37.160
And it's today!

00:14:37.830 --> 00:14:40.890
Kotecchan is already in 
her uniform, so let's go!

00:14:40.890 --> 00:14:42.040
What?!

00:14:42.040 --> 00:14:43.500
No, wait...

00:14:46.230 --> 00:14:47.990
<b>Home Ec Room</b>

00:14:51.080 --> 00:14:53.670
I didn't say it was a cheer request.

00:14:55.090 --> 00:14:57.370
This is the president of the home ec club.

00:14:58.080 --> 00:15:00.560
Sorry to ask you to come here so suddenly.

00:15:00.560 --> 00:15:03.750
It's not exactly a cheer request, 
but we'd like your help.

00:15:04.800 --> 00:15:08.190
Does this not work unless it's 
specifically a cheer request?

00:15:08.190 --> 00:15:09.510
Work?

00:15:09.900 --> 00:15:12.190
I heard when you make a request 
to the Cheer Association,

00:15:12.190 --> 00:15:13.870
any wish will come true,

00:15:13.870 --> 00:15:15.360
be it relationships,

00:15:15.360 --> 00:15:16.600
studying,

00:15:16.600 --> 00:15:18.140
or sports.

00:15:18.140 --> 00:15:20.640
What the heck? Who did you hear that from?

00:15:21.190 --> 00:15:25.450
Apparently Akitsune's friend 
had her wish come true.

00:15:25.450 --> 00:15:26.490
Friend?

00:15:26.490 --> 00:15:27.900
Really, now?

00:15:28.340 --> 00:15:33.040
It doesn't exactly work like that, 
but we'd be happy to help out!

00:15:33.040 --> 00:15:36.410
But is there anything we can do to help?

00:15:36.790 --> 00:15:44.790
<b>High School
Cooking Contest</b>

00:15:37.010 --> 00:15:42.100
We'd like some help in deciding the 
menu for the upcoming cooking contest.

00:15:42.630 --> 00:15:44.790
Just sample some dishes 
and give us your opinions.

00:15:44.790 --> 00:15:49.950
But it'll all be based on 
our personal opinions.

00:15:49.950 --> 00:15:51.130
Is that all right?

00:15:51.130 --> 00:15:53.160
Oh, no problem.

00:15:53.160 --> 00:15:57.010
There's four of you, so that's enough to 
cover the tastes of the rest of humanity.

00:15:57.010 --> 00:15:59.140
Y-You think so?

00:16:00.550 --> 00:16:02.770
We have a variety of samples.

00:16:03.360 --> 00:16:07.520
The first dish is rolled 
cabbage in cream sauce.

00:16:07.520 --> 00:16:09.770
Wow, that looks really good!

00:16:09.770 --> 00:16:12.260
What do you think? 
Give us your honest opinions.

00:16:13.560 --> 00:16:15.030
Wait, already?

00:16:15.360 --> 00:16:20.490
Um... I'm sorry. May I go change?

00:16:20.490 --> 00:16:22.250
I feel so out of place.

00:16:22.250 --> 00:16:24.330
Oh, sorry, Kotecchan!

00:16:26.970 --> 00:16:29.300
The second dish is seafood doria.

00:16:34.450 --> 00:16:36.150
It's so good!

00:16:37.000 --> 00:16:39.930
Our third dish is gratin 
with seasonal vegetables.

00:16:42.290 --> 00:16:44.190
This is delicious, too!

00:16:44.520 --> 00:16:49.690
The fourth dish is our special original 
Kaminoki High School carbonara.

00:16:50.560 --> 00:16:52.820
Ooh, I love this, too!

00:16:53.380 --> 00:16:54.700
So good!

00:16:55.160 --> 00:16:56.570
Yummy!

00:16:56.890 --> 00:16:59.200
So good!

00:16:59.200 --> 00:17:02.280
Um... What's that thing you keep doing?

00:17:02.280 --> 00:17:03.710
This is a high V!

00:17:05.280 --> 00:17:09.590
Don't worry about them.
It's basically become a habit.

00:17:13.060 --> 00:17:15.930
Is there anything that you really like?

00:17:17.190 --> 00:17:18.570
Beans, I guess?

00:17:18.570 --> 00:17:20.350
Beans? Just beans?

00:17:20.900 --> 00:17:22.910
Hatoya-san likes beans...

00:17:22.910 --> 00:17:26.100
So does that mean Sawatari-san likes...

00:17:29.510 --> 00:17:31.910
Could you not make fun of me?!

00:17:33.440 --> 00:17:35.610
Hatoya-san, have some red bean soup.

00:17:37.390 --> 00:17:39.100
Is that another arm motion?

00:17:39.100 --> 00:17:40.540
Yes. That's a clap.

00:17:40.540 --> 00:17:43.240
Uh, I think she's just happy.

00:17:43.680 --> 00:17:45.320
Have some sesame soy spinach.

00:17:47.840 --> 00:17:52.280
<i>Th-The spinach clearly hasn't 
been rinsed thoroughly...</i>

00:17:52.280 --> 00:17:53.750
<i>I need to tell her.</i>

00:17:54.640 --> 00:17:57.500
U-Um... This spinach...

00:17:57.500 --> 00:18:00.220
Oh, I made that!

00:18:00.220 --> 00:18:01.820
Well? How is it?

00:18:03.850 --> 00:18:06.730
It tastes very earthy.

00:18:07.000 --> 00:18:09.270
You're not hiding your honesty very well...

00:18:10.850 --> 00:18:14.110
You're all so good at cooking.

00:18:14.410 --> 00:18:15.990
I know, right?

00:18:16.470 --> 00:18:20.990
Cooking is a lot of fun. It's also great 
training to become the perfect wife.

00:18:21.260 --> 00:18:22.240
Wife?

00:18:22.950 --> 00:18:25.250
Do you already have someone 
you're going to marry?

00:18:31.520 --> 00:18:33.710
You're pretty frank, aren't you?

00:18:33.710 --> 00:18:37.760
It's more like whatever I'm thinking just
 comes naturally out of my mouth...

00:18:38.140 --> 00:18:40.190
So you're probably like Kohane.

00:18:40.190 --> 00:18:42.270
She says whatever's on her mind

00:18:42.270 --> 00:18:44.410
and forgets everything 
after taking three steps.

00:18:44.410 --> 00:18:45.060
Peep?!

00:18:45.400 --> 00:18:47.560
Hmm... I don't think we're the same.

00:18:47.560 --> 00:18:48.940
See?! You're doing it again!

00:18:52.100 --> 00:18:56.070
This is so amazing. It must be 
a lot of fun cooking together.

00:18:56.070 --> 00:18:58.080
Oh, are you interested?

00:18:58.080 --> 00:19:01.450
You get better really fast 
when you cook every week.

00:19:01.770 --> 00:19:05.580
Wow, it's so nice that you can 
have fun learning something.

00:19:09.160 --> 00:19:11.640
What's wrong with Arima-san?

00:19:11.640 --> 00:19:13.080
Did she not like the dishes?

00:19:13.620 --> 00:19:17.530
Oh, that face means she's thinking 
Kohane might quit cheerleading

00:19:17.530 --> 00:19:19.640
to join the home ec club.

00:19:20.200 --> 00:19:21.660
Hizume, Uki!

00:19:22.520 --> 00:19:25.110
Cooking seems like a lot of fun, so...

00:19:26.360 --> 00:19:28.680
Let's have our own training camp!

00:19:28.270 --> 00:19:31.350
<b>Is the base
 white miso?</b>

00:19:28.680 --> 00:19:31.350
They called you "the cast iron base," right?

00:19:33.360 --> 00:19:35.980
The training camp shouldn't 
be for cooking practice!

00:19:36.920 --> 00:19:39.050
And it's "the impregnable base."

00:19:44.150 --> 00:19:47.370
Okay, I think I managed to
 gather all your opinions.

00:19:47.890 --> 00:19:50.910
This is our way of saying thank you.

00:19:52.040 --> 00:19:55.340
Wait, wait! All we did was eat 
and give you our opinions!

00:19:55.340 --> 00:19:57.170
I'd feel bad eating this!

00:19:57.630 --> 00:19:59.120
Kohane, you're drooling.

00:20:00.520 --> 00:20:03.550
You see, we received a request, too...

00:20:03.880 --> 00:20:05.680
From the basketball team.

00:20:06.400 --> 00:20:09.240
They wanted to thank you for 
cheering them on the other day,

00:20:09.240 --> 00:20:12.490
but they didn't think they could do much.

00:20:13.430 --> 00:20:15.190
Plus, their captain is really shy.

00:20:15.190 --> 00:20:17.560
Basketball-senpai...

00:20:17.560 --> 00:20:19.190
Thank us?

00:20:19.530 --> 00:20:21.000
All they'd have to do is

00:20:21.000 --> 00:20:25.320
add "The Cheer Association is amazing" 
to the end of every sentence.

00:20:25.320 --> 00:20:27.330
Learn to catch a clue, Hizume!

00:20:35.700 --> 00:20:37.840
I think I can finally understand all that.

00:20:38.140 --> 00:20:40.620
I love this so much.

00:20:40.620 --> 00:20:43.720
Perhaps it's because you made 
this especially for us.

00:20:44.060 --> 00:20:45.790
I see...

00:20:45.790 --> 00:20:48.830
Maybe we can put our hearts 
into our cooking more when

00:20:48.830 --> 00:20:50.710
we know exactly who we're cooking for.

00:20:51.830 --> 00:20:53.820
Here you go, Arima-san.

00:20:54.760 --> 00:20:57.320
Did you give this any thought at all?

00:20:57.320 --> 00:21:00.020
Just cutting it into pretty shapes 
doesn't make it better!

00:21:00.480 --> 00:21:04.600
More importantly, we have to 
go thank Basketball-senpai!

00:21:05.220 --> 00:21:07.460
But it'd be a waste not to eat everything!

00:21:08.500 --> 00:21:10.660
Thanks for the food! Okay!

00:21:11.400 --> 00:21:14.160
You don't have to wash the dishes, just go!

00:21:17.080 --> 00:21:18.080
Go!

00:21:18.510 --> 00:21:19.590
Captain!

00:21:21.220 --> 00:21:22.000
Yes!

00:21:22.000 --> 00:21:23.550
Basketball-senpai!

00:21:23.550 --> 00:21:26.800
We heard your feelings loud and clear!

00:21:28.020 --> 00:21:29.550
Wh-What are you talking about?

00:21:29.890 --> 00:21:31.420
Oh, come on, now.

00:21:31.420 --> 00:21:34.640
The president of the home ec 
club told us all about it.

00:21:34.640 --> 00:21:36.190
I don't know what you're talking about.

00:21:36.650 --> 00:21:40.320
Okay, we're going to do a cheer 
to thank you for your thanks!

00:21:40.320 --> 00:21:41.720
Listen to me!

00:21:41.720 --> 00:21:45.820
Please! Just let me express these 
overflowing emotions with a cheer!

00:21:45.820 --> 00:21:49.570
But we're just doing a normal practice today.

00:21:49.570 --> 00:21:52.330
Please, Basketball-senpai.

00:21:52.650 --> 00:21:55.280
<i>She's usually the one holding her back...</i>

00:21:55.280 --> 00:21:56.670
<i>They're that grateful?</i>

00:21:57.330 --> 00:21:59.740
I need to move around as soon as possible!

00:21:59.740 --> 00:22:01.590
If I don't, my body's gonna regret it!

00:22:02.000 --> 00:22:04.060
How much did you eat?

00:23:38.390 --> 00:23:41.940
Next time: "Super Exciting 
Double Base Thigh Stand!"
